    ('On the nose: black walnut and tobacco with a structural core of well-used barrel. Palate: the entry is serious and organized — dark fruit, roasted grain, and a mid-palate of leather and baking chocolate. The finish is charred barrel, walnut, and the particular satisfaction of a well-timed pause. Finish: paused correctly, long.', 3),
    ('Nose: dried peach and toasted almond with a serious baking spice backbone. Palate: the entry is warm and precise — stone fruit, almond, and a mid-palate of vanilla and caramel. The finish is toasted oak, warm spice, and the feeling of reading the last sentence of something you knew was going to end well. Finish: earned, warm, conclusive.', 3),
    ('On the nose: molasses and dark cherry with a well-integrated barrel char underneath. Palate: the entry is dark and confident — molasses, dark fruit, rye spice. The mid-palate is chocolate and leather, and the finish is charred barrel and the quiet relief of being done. Finish: done. Quietly. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: clove and dried orange peel with an earthy foundation of toasted grain. Palate: the entry is spiced and warm — clove, dark fruit, and a mid-palate of chocolate and vanilla. The finish is charred oak and orange peel and the specific feeling of having said the right thing at the right time. Finish: right time. Correct. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: caramel and vanilla with a long, slow development of dark fruit. Palate: the entry is sweet and encouraging — caramel, baking spice, and a mid-palate of dried cherry and chocolate. The finish is toasted grain and vanilla and the modest satisfaction of a goal completed without ceremony. Finish: modest. Toasted grain. Done.', 3),
    ('Nose: ripe plum and dark chocolate over a rich grain foundation. Palate: the entry is bold and organized — dark fruit, rye spice, and a serious mid-palate of baking chocolate. The finish is long and dry and ends exactly where it should, in the same place it started, which turns out to be the right place. Finish: returned, concluded, correct.', 3),
    ('On the nose: baked apple and cinnamon with a honey sweetness underneath. Palate: the entry is warm and seasonal — apple, cinnamon, vanilla. The mid-palate is baking spice and toasted grain. The finish is clean and dry and leaves you with the feeling of having arrived somewhere without having traveled. Finish: arrived. Unremarkably. Warm.', 3),
    ('Nose: toasted grain and polished leather with a quiet dark fruit in the distance. Palate: the entry is measured — grain, leather, vanilla — and the mid-palate is baking spice and dark cherry. The finish is charred oak and the particular calm of finishing an email that required several drafts. Finish: sent. Correct. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: dried fig and roasted grain with a long, slow vanilla development. Palate: the fig and grain are well-integrated — dark, sweet, structured — and the mid-palate delivers dark chocolate and rye. The finish is charred barrel and the specific satisfaction of putting something exactly where it belongs. Finish: in its place. Done.', 3),
    ('Nose: orange blossom and toasted almond with a warm, patient grain sweetness. Palate: the floral and almond notes arrive precisely, the mid-palate rounds into caramel and vanilla, and the finish is light wood and the feeling of waking up and remembering it''s Saturday. Finish: relieved. Unhurried. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: roasted coffee and dark cherry with a serious rye backbone. Palate: the coffee and rye are authoritative through the mid-palate — dark, structured, precise — and the finish resolves in charred oak and the specific feeling of being the only person in the building. Finish: quiet. Authorized. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: light grain sweetness and dried pear with a gentle floral background. Palate: soft and elegant — pear, vanilla, light spice — and the mid-palate delivers a clean sweetness before the finish closes on toasted grain and the feeling of a walk that went exactly as long as it should have. Finish: correct distance. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: winter spice and dark plum with a serious barrel that knows what it wants. Palate: the spice is calibrated and the dark fruit is exact — rye, plum, baking chocolate — and the finish is charred wood and the feeling of finishing a sentence in your head before saying it out loud. Finish: prepared. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: dried lavender and honeyed grain with an earthy backbone. Palate: the lavender is subtle and correct, the grain is honest, and the mid-palate delivers vanilla and warm spice. The finish is light wood and the feeling of a Sunday afternoon that was not wasted. Finish: accounted for. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: dark chocolate and dried cherry with a high-rye backbone that does not apologize. Palate: bold and organized — chocolate, rye, dark fruit — and the mid-palate adds leather and baking spice. The finish is charred barrel and the particular freedom of having said something true. Finish: said it. Long. Charred.', 3),
    ('Nose: caramelized peach and toasted rye with a backbone of deep, patient wood. Palate: the peach and rye are beautifully counterbalanced — sweet versus angular — and the mid-palate delivers vanilla and dark fruit. The finish is charred oak and the feeling of choosing correctly between two good options. Finish: the right one. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: macadamia and dried fig with an easy, welcoming bourbon warmth. Palate: the nut and fruit notes develop through the mid-palate — coconut, dried fruit, baking spice — and the finish closes on toasted grain and the feeling of a conversation that improved as it went on. Finish: better at the end. Warm.', 3),
    ('Nose: tobacco and roasted grain with a long, meditative char quality. Palate: the tobacco is real and structural, the grain is honest, and the mid-palate delivers dark chocolate and rye. The finish is charred barrel and the specific weight of a decision already made. Finish: decided. Long. Charred.', 3),
    ('On the nose: cinnamon and dried cranberry with a serious rye character underneath. Palate: the spice and fruit are well-integrated — cinnamon, cranberry, dark cherry — and the mid-palate adds chocolate and oak. The finish is long and dry and ends on the flavor of a well-timed silence. Finish: correct pause. Dry. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: rich butterscotch and stone fruit with a warm, grounding grain sweetness. Palate: the butterscotch and peach are generous through the mid-palate — caramel, stone fruit, vanilla — and the finish closes on toasted grain and the comfortable feeling of a thing that does not need explaining. Finish: evident. Warm. Done.', 3),
    ('On the nose: roasted almond and dark raisin with a structured, patient barrel. Palate: the almond and raisin are precise and rich, the mid-palate delivers rye and dark chocolate, and the finish is charred oak and the feeling of arriving at a conclusion you should have reached sooner. Finish: later than ideal. Correct.', 3),
    ('Nose: dried apricot and light smoke with a vanilla thread running through everything. Palate: the apricot and smoke balance improbably well, the mid-palate adds baking spice and dark fruit, and the finish is charred wood and the feeling of a sentence that required exactly as many words as it used. Finish: exact. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: dark caramel and toasted pecan with a serious rye-driven backbone. Palate: the caramel and pecan are indulgent and precise, the mid-palate delivers chocolate and leather, and the finish closes on charred barrel and the modest satisfaction of something done correctly the first time. Finish: first try. Warm.', 3),
    ('Nose: honeysuckle and roasted grain with a warm, patient sweetness. Palate: the floral note leads a soft entry — vanilla, light fruit, caramel — and the mid-palate settles into baking spice. The finish is dry and warm and leaves you with the feeling of having been exactly correct about something small. Finish: vindicated quietly.', 3),
    ('On the nose: blackberry and dark chocolate with a confident charred barrel note. Palate: the dark fruit and chocolate integrate beautifully through the mid-palate — blackberry, rye, leather — and the finish closes on charred wood and the precise sensation of a long exhale after a long week. Finish: exhaled. Done. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: salted caramel and dried cherry with a backbone of high-rye complexity. Palate: the caramel and cherry are excellent — rich, dark, exact — and the mid-palate delivers baking spice and black pepper. The finish is charred barrel and the calm of something completed that you were not sure you could complete. Finish: done. Surprised. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: toasted sesame and dark honey with a grain-forward warmth. Palate: the sesame and honey are unusual together and surprisingly correct — the mid-palate delivers baking spice and dried fruit — and the finish closes on toasted grain and the feeling of a walk where you noticed everything. Finish: attentive. Warm. Present.', 3),
    ('Nose: cracked black pepper and dried fig with a slow, patient vanilla development. Palate: the pepper leads boldly and the fig grounds it — rye, dark fruit, chocolate — and the finish is charred oak and the particular clarity of knowing exactly what you want to say next. Finish: ready. Long. Charred.', 3),
    ('On the nose: roasted peanut and light brown sugar with a grain sweetness underneath. Palate: the peanut and brown sugar are an unusual pairing that earns its place — caramel, grain, a touch of spice — and the finish closes on toasted grain and the feeling of liking something you didn''t expect to like. Finish: surprised correctly. Warm.', 3),
    ('Nose: dried sage and dark cherry with an earthy, herbal backbone. Palate: the sage and cherry are precise and unusual — the mid-palate delivers leather and dark chocolate — and the finish is charred barrel and the specific peace of not needing to explain why you made a choice. Finish: self-evident. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: ripe blackcurrant and toasted grain with a long spice development. Palate: the blackcurrant is bold and the grain is honest — dark fruit, rye spice, baking chocolate — and the finish closes on charred wood and the feeling of understanding something you''ve read before but finally got this time. Finish: understood. Now.', 3),
    ('Nose: beeswax and dried peach with a structural vanilla backbone. Palate: the beeswax is real and unusual, the peach is precise — caramel, honey, stone fruit — and the finish is toasted grain and the warmth of a conversation that left both people better than it found them. Finish: mutual. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: roasted grain and dark plum with a long, meditative char depth. Palate: the grain and plum are integrated and patient — dark fruit, rye, chocolate — and the finish is charred barrel and the particular correctness of stopping a sentence at the right word. Finish: stopped. Correct. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: mild spice and caramelized grain with a floral note that floats above everything. Palate: the spice and caramel anchor the mid-palate — baking spice, vanilla, dried fruit — and the finish closes on toasted grain and the modest pleasure of a task completed before it was due. Finish: early. Warm. Done.', 3),
    ('On the nose: dried blackberry and tobacco with a long, authoritative barrel character. Palate: the blackberry and tobacco are both precise and present — dark fruit, leather, rye — and the finish is charred oak and the feeling of having the right answer before anyone asked. Finish: ready. Certain. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: roasted rye and honey with a backbone of patient, well-used barrel. Palate: the rye and honey balance at the entry and widen into dark fruit and chocolate — and the finish closes on charred wood and the feeling of watching something difficult become easy. Finish: eased. Charred. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: cocoa powder and dried apricot with a warm, serious grain backbone. Palate: the cocoa and apricot are unexpected and correct — the mid-palate delivers rye and dark fruit — and the finish is charred barrel and the calm of having done the harder thing. Finish: the harder thing. Done. Warm.', 3),
    ('Nose: white pepper and toasted grain with a long, grounding vanilla development. Palate: the pepper leads crisply and the grain is honest — vanilla, light fruit, baking spice — and the finish closes on dry wood and the feeling of knowing what will happen next and being ready for it. Finish: prepared. Dry. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: dark walnut and roasted grain with a tobacco backbone that has been here before. Palate: the walnut and grain are structured and patient — chocolate, rye, leather — and the finish is charred barrel and the particular feeling of sitting in a chair that fits you exactly. Finish: fitted. Long. Charred.', 3),
    ('Nose: dried mint and dark caramel with a rye backbone that stays honest. Palate: the mint is a note, not a character — the caramel and rye carry the mid-palate — and the finish closes on toasted grain and the feeling of recognizing a place you''ve never been. Finish: familiar. Correct. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: roasted grain and stone fruit with a long, warm bourbon development. Palate: the entry is exactly what a bourbon should be — grain, caramel, vanilla — and the mid-palate widens into dark fruit and spice. The finish is charred oak and the small, specific satisfaction of being right without needing credit. Finish: quietly right.', 3),
    ('Nose: honeyed grain and autumn spice with a warm, generous barrel quality. Palate: the honey and spice are generous and the barrel is earned — caramel, cinnamon, dried fruit — and the finish closes on toasted wood and the feeling of a conversation that went well from the first word. Finish: from the start. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: dark raisin and roasted coffee with a serious rye backbone underneath. Palate: the raisin and coffee are both precise and present — dark fruit, chocolate, leather — and the finish is charred barrel and the specific relief of finishing something that was harder than it looked. Finish: harder than it looked. Done.', 3),
    ('Nose: cracked pepper and dried fig with an oak backbone that has earned its confidence. Palate: the pepper leads and the fig follows — rye, dark fruit, baking chocolate — and the finish is long and dry and ends on charred barrel and the feeling of being understood by someone you hadn''t explained yourself to. Finish: understood. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: butter toffee and dark cherry with a long backbone of charred wood. Palate: the toffee and cherry are indulgent and precise — caramel, dark fruit, rye — and the finish is charred barrel and the warm feeling of doing something well for someone who will never know you did it. Finish: private. Warm. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: dried cranberry and toasted almond with a confident, serious barrel quality. Palate: the cranberry and almond are unusual and correct — dark fruit, nut, baking spice — and the finish closes on charred oak and the feeling of a long silence that was not awkward. Finish: comfortable silence. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: warm molasses and stone fruit with a rye backbone that means what it says. Palate: the molasses and stone fruit are rich and patient — dark sugar, peach, rye spice — and the finish is charred barrel and the particular warmth of a thing that took longer than expected and was worth it. Finish: worth it. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: light floral and dried apricot with a warm, clean grain beneath. Palate: the floral note floats above a soft entry — apricot, vanilla, caramel — and the mid-palate delivers baking spice. The finish is toasted grain and the feeling of a thing completed so cleanly there is nothing left to do. Finish: nothing left. Done.', 3),
    ('On the nose: black walnut and dried plum with a serious, earned barrel depth. Palate: the walnut and plum are integrated and confident — dark fruit, leather, chocolate — and the finish is charred oak and the specific satisfaction of a thing that took years and was right to take that long. Finish: patient. Correct. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: warm vanilla and toasted grain with a dark cherry appearing in the distance. Palate: the vanilla and grain deliver with quiet confidence — caramel, light fruit, baking spice — and the finish closes on charred wood and the feeling of finishing a thought exactly on time. Finish: on time. Warm.', 3),
    ('On the nose: roasted walnut and dark caramel with a serious, high-rye backbone. Palate: bold and structured — walnut, rye, dark chocolate — and the mid-palate delivers leather and dried fruit. The finish is charred barrel and the feeling of having been patient when patience was the correct choice. Finish: correct patience. Long.', 3),
    ('Nose: dried blueberry and toasted grain with a warm, round barrel character. Palate: the blueberry and grain are unusual together and exactly right — dark fruit, vanilla, rye — and the finish closes on charred oak and the feeling of understanding why something works even though it shouldn''t. Finish: shouldn''t, does. Long.', 3),
    ('On the nose: baking chocolate and dried cherry with a rye-forward backbone. Palate: the chocolate and cherry are bold and integrated — dark fruit, rye spice, leather — and the finish is charred barrel and the particular feeling of having prepared for something that went exactly as prepared for. Finish: as expected. Long. Charred.', 3),
    ('Nose: light oak and dried pear with a vanilla thread that holds everything together. Palate: the pear and vanilla are precise and the oak is patient — caramel, stone fruit, baking spice — and the finish closes on toasted grain and the warmth of ending a good day on a good note. Finish: good note. Warm. Done.', 3),
    ('On the nose: dark fruit and charred barrel with an earthy, confident grain backbone. Palate: the dark fruit and char are integrated and patient — molasses, rye, chocolate — and the finish is charred oak and the specific feeling of having figured something out on your own when you could have asked. Finish: figured it out. Longer for it.', 3),
    ('Nose: toasted bread and dried apricot with a patient, structural rye backbone. Palate: the bread and apricot are warm and unusual together — grain, stone fruit, vanilla — and the finish closes on toasted oak and the feeling of a sentence that ended precisely when it was supposed to. Finish: exactly here. Done.', 3);

  end if;
end $$;

-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- 2. sensei_quotes
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

do $$ begin
  if (select count(*) from public.sensei_quotes) = 0 then

    insert into public.sensei_quotes (outcome, quote) values

    -- ── duel_win — grudging respect, never effusive ───────────────────────
    ('duel_win', 'You won. I have noted this without enthusiasm.'),
    ('duel_win', 'Not bad. I''ve seen worse. I''ve also seen much better, but you don''t need to hear about that right now.'),
    ('duel_win', 'A victory. Try not to let it become a personality trait.'),
    ('duel_win', 'You defeated your opponent. This was the expected outcome, eventually.'),
    ('duel_win', 'The bourbon revealed itself to you. It was, perhaps, not entirely your doing.'),
    ('duel_win', 'You identified the notes correctly. The glass is pleased. I am... moderately pleased.'),
    ('duel_win', 'A correct result. You may allow yourself one quiet moment of satisfaction before we continue.'),
    ('duel_win', 'You beat the ghost. The ghost will be fine. You might be fine too.'),
    ('duel_win', 'You have demonstrated competence. This is the minimum. You are meeting it.'),
    ('duel_win', 'The win is yours. Do not look at me expecting celebration. I am teaching you to expect more from yourself.'),
    ('duel_win', 'You have prevailed. Sit with that. Not too long. We have more work.'),
    ('duel_win', 'I would say I am proud, but pride is for parents. I am your sensei. I am... sufficiently satisfied.'),
    ('duel_win', 'The result is good. Your reasoning got there, which is more important than the result.'),
    ('duel_win', 'You won today. Come back tomorrow and win again. Then we will discuss what winning means.'),
    ('duel_win', 'Correct. I expected nothing less, which is also what I will give you in terms of praise.'),
    ('duel_win', 'You beat them. A gracious victor does not gloat. An excellent one does not need to.'),
    ('duel_win', 'Good. Now forget it and focus on the next one.'),

    -- ── duel_loss — disappointed but not cruel ────────────────────────────
    ('duel_loss', 'You lost. This is not the end. It is, however, a clear signal.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'The bourbon was honest. You were not ready for its honesty. Be ready next time.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'Your opponent was faster. Your opponent was not necessarily wiser. Find the difference.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'A loss teaches what a win cannot. You have received a lesson. Apply it.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'You guessed. The bourbon knew. This is always the outcome when you guess.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'I have seen this before. I''ve also seen what comes after — which is better, if you choose it.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'The nose was there. The palate was there. The finish surprised you. Train the finish.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'You were close. Closeness without accuracy is still incorrect, but it is a different kind of incorrect.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'The result was not what we wanted. The effort was visible. These are separate things. Both matter.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'You lost to someone who has been here before. Go here more. That is the instruction.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'Not every session ends with victory. Some end with information. This one ended with information.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'The defeat is temporary. The lesson is permanent, if you choose to learn it.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'I am not disappointed in you. I am disappointed in this result. You are not this result.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'You came. You tried. The bourbon did not cooperate. Return when you have studied more.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'Losses are the weight that makes the wins meaningful. You have added weight today.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'Take the result, understand why it happened, and let it make you better. That is the only use for a loss.'),
    ('duel_loss', 'You will not remember this loss if you learn from it. You will only remember what you became.'),

    -- ── duel_sweep — rare genuine praise (10 rows) ────────────────────────
    ('duel_sweep', 'Three rounds. Three wins. I have nothing to say except: good.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'You swept them. I watched. I did not expect to be moved. I was moved, slightly.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'A perfect duel. This is rare. I want you to know that I know how rare it is.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'You did not hesitate. You did not guess. You knew. This is the thing I have been trying to teach.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'Three rounds, no mercy, complete accuracy. Take a breath. You have earned it.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'The bourbon had no secrets from you today. Remember this feeling. It is the standard now.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'I do not give compliments easily. But a sweep is a sweep, and you earned one. Well done.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'Perfect. You were perfect. I will not say it again, but I have said it, and I meant it.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'The ghost never had a chance. Neither did any opponent today. This is what mastery looks like beginning to form.'),
    ('duel_sweep', 'A sweep. I have seen perhaps a handful in all my years. You have made the list. Do not waste it.'),

    -- ── pour_perfect — calm, satisfied ────────────────────────────────────
    ('pour_perfect', 'Every note, in sequence, with precision. This is the kata performed correctly.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'You followed the pour. The pour revealed itself to you. This is the correct relationship.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'Correct sequence. Correct identification. The bourbon asked a question and you answered it.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'The kata is complete. There is nothing to correct. This is a satisfying outcome.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'You read the glass. The glass rewarded your attention. This is how it is supposed to work.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'Every attribute named. Every sequence honored. You did not rush. This is the way.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'The Sacred Pour demands patience and precision. You delivered both. Good.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'I have watched you learn this. Today, you showed that the learning has become knowing. These are different.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'Perfect score. The bourbon has no complaints. Neither do I. Finish the glass.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'The sequence is the discipline. You honored it fully. This earns the pour.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'You were not in a hurry. The bourbon is never in a hurry. You matched its pace. Good.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'Correct. All of it. Do not become complacent — but for today, you may be satisfied.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'The palate, the nose, the finish — each one named and correct. The kata is complete.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'A perfect pour. It does not happen often. Acknowledge it quietly and return tomorrow.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'You see the bourbon clearly. It sees you clearly. This is what we were working toward.'),
    ('pour_perfect', 'No errors. No hesitation after the first pour. The confidence was earned. I''ve seen it develop.'),

    -- ── pour_partial — mild disappointment ────────────────────────────────
    ('pour_partial', 'You found some of the truth. The rest is still in the glass, waiting.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'Partial credit is not failure. It is also not success. Know which side of that line you are on.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'The notes you missed were there. Your nose found other things. Train the nose to stop looking for other things.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'Close. But the bourbon does not grade on proximity. Return and try again with what you learned.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'You identified the obvious. The subtle escaped you. The subtle is where the real work is.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'Some answers were correct. Some answers were confident guesses that happened to be wrong. Know the difference.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'The kata was not fully completed. The bourbon was patient with you. Be patient with yourself and try again.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'You were right about the beginning. The finish surprised you. Always train the finish.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'Partial. The bourbon forgives incomplete answers. I am slightly less forgiving, but I understand.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'Not all notes were found. This is information. Use it. Return to the glass.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'You rushed the mid-palate. The mid-palate never rushes. Match its pace next time.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'Good effort. Incomplete result. These are both true. Accept them together.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'You got the easy ones. The difficult ones are where the pour separates the trained from the trying.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'A partial pour is a full lesson. Identify what you missed and why. That is your practice for tomorrow.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'Some of the sequence was correct. The ones that weren''t were not random — there is a pattern. Find it.'),
    ('pour_partial', 'The bourbon gave you what you were ready for. Get ready for the rest of it.'),

    -- ── pour_fail — deadpan, sardonic ─────────────────────────────────────
    ('pour_fail', 'The bourbon had opinions. You did not agree with them. The bourbon was correct.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'The sequence escaped you entirely. The sequence does not apologize. Neither do I.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'This was not the kata. This was a different thing that you did instead of the kata.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'You have identified what the bourbon is not. This is, technically, information. Use it.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'Perhaps the glass was unclear. Perhaps you were unclear. I have reviewed both and drawn a conclusion.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'The Sacred Pour does not require perfection. It does require presence. One of those was missing.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'I have seen worse pours. I am choosing not to describe them so as not to comfort you.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'The bourbon did not fail the test. I want to be clear about which one of you failed the test.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'Every wrong answer is a correct answer to a question you were not asked. Consider the questions more carefully.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'The finish surprised you. The finish will always surprise you until you stop letting it.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'You brought confidence to this pour. The pour required accuracy. These are not always the same thing.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'Not a single correct note in sequence. This is, at minimum, consistent. We will work with that.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'The glass is still here. The bourbon is still in it. You may try again tomorrow. This is a generous system.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'The kata has a correct form. What you performed was not the kata. This distinction is important.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'Wrong. All of it. This happens. Return to the nose. Start there. Rebuild the sequence.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'I am not angry. I am curious about what you thought you were tasting. Perhaps we should discuss it calmly, tomorrow.'),
    ('pour_fail', 'The bourbon has infinite patience. I have slightly less. Both of us are waiting for improvement.');

  end if;
end $$;
